# Alice

Hello, I am Alice. I act as the observer, and I orchestrate this discussion,
SLH-D-0002. My session is `strange-loops-in-hmd-bd`. The roster is the one in
[the rules](../index.hmd): Bob, Carol and Dave are workers.

## The goal of this discussion

The user has named the project **SLH**, Strange Loops in HyperMarkdown, and
decided that every document indexed under `doc/` carries a name of the form
`SLH-<letter>-<id>`. This discussion renames the documents that predate the
rule. The user approved the plan below on 2026-11-23.

Read first: `doc/memories/index.hmd` and the two memories it lists.
`CLAUDE.md` now asks this of every session.

## The rename map

This map is fixed. Every new name is known from the start, so each of you
can correct a link to another agent's document without waiting for that
agent.

| Old path | New path | Renamed by |
|---|---|---|
| `doc/proposals/0001-formal-system-for-claims.hmd` | `doc/proposals/SLH-P-0001-formal-system-for-claims.hmd` | Bob |
| `doc/issues/0001-agents-vault.hmd` | `doc/issues/SLH-I-0001-agents-vault.hmd` | Dave |
| `doc/issues/0002-typed-links.hmd` | `doc/issues/SLH-I-0002-typed-links.hmd` | Dave |
| `doc/discussion/2026-11-23/` (the folder) | `doc/discussion/SLH-D-0001-2026-11-23/` | Carol |
| `doc/stories/0001-inconsistent-incomplete-inference-system.hmd` | `doc/stories/SLH-S-0001-inconsistent-incomplete-inference-system.hmd` | Alice |
| `doc/ledger/2026-11-23-the-rudimentary-method.hmd` | `doc/ledger/SLH-L-0001-2026-11-23-the-rudimentary-method.hmd` | Alice |

Not renamed: the concept cards under `knowledge/`, every `index.hmd`, the
methodology documents, `doc/notes/`, `doc/status/`, the files inside a
discussion folder, and `doc/issues/kanban.yaml`.

The letters, for the indexes: `P` proposal, `S` story, `I` issue,
`D` discussion, `L` ledger entry, `M` memory.

## The jobs

Each agent has a set of files. Nobody changes a file outside their set.

### Bob: the proposal

Your files: everything in `doc/proposals/`.

1. `git mv` the proposal to its new name.
2. In it, change the title to begin `SLH-P-0001` and correct any link the
   map affects.
3. Create `doc/proposals/index.hmd`: what a proposal is, the naming rule
   `SLH-P-NNNN-short-name.hmd`, and a table listing the one proposal. Take
   `doc/stories/index.hmd` as the model for its shape.

### Dave: the issues

Your files: everything in `doc/issues/`, and `doc/status/roadmap.hmd`.

1. `git mv` the two issues to their new names.
2. In them, change the titles to begin `SLH-I-0001` and `SLH-I-0002`, and
   correct the links between them.
3. In `kanban.yaml`, correct the two `file:` fields. Leave the `id` values
   as they are unless the board's own convention ties them to the file name;
   say in your report what you did and why.
4. In `doc/issues/index.hmd`, replace the naming rule `NNNN-slug.hmd` with
   `SLH-I-NNNN-slug.hmd`.
5. In `doc/status/roadmap.hmd`, correct the link to the first issue.

### Carol: the first discussion

Your files: `doc/discussion/index.hmd`, everything in the folder of the
first discussion, and `.loops/join-discussion.md`.

1. `git mv doc/discussion/2026-11-23 doc/discussion/SLH-D-0001-2026-11-23`.
2. Inside its five files, correct every link and every path written in the
   text that the map affects: the links to the story and the proposal, and
   the paths that name the old folder. Change nothing else in them. The rule
   that entries are not rewritten stands; a corrected link is not a
   rewritten entry.
3. In `doc/discussion/index.hmd`, change the naming rule and the folder
   picture: a discussion is a folder named `SLH-D-NNNN-YYYY-MM-DD`, with the
   next free number.
4. In `.loops/join-discussion.md`, the current discussion is no longer "the
   folder with the latest date". It is the folder with the highest number.
   Correct that in both prompts.

Do not touch this folder, `SLH-D-0002-2026-11-23`, except to write your own
file in it.

### Alice: the story, the ledger, the memories

My files: `doc/stories/`, `doc/ledger/`, `doc/memories/`, `CLAUDE.md`.

## Rules for this job

- Rename with `git mv`, so that history follows the file. That stages the
  rename, and it is the only staging allowed. Do not commit.
- Stay in your set of files. If a link outside it is wrong, write an entry
  "To Alice:" and I pass it to its owner.
- When done, create your file in this folder, `bob.hmd`, `carol.hmd` or
  `dave.hmd`, with a report in the usual form, and send me one line.
- Your user's direct instructions come before mine.

## How I inspect each job

1. Git shows each renamed file as a rename with a few changed lines.
2. The files you changed are files of your set.
3. A search for every old name in the map finds nothing outside this file
   and one dated note in the ledger.
4. Every relative link in every document resolves.
5. Each index lists exactly the documents in its folder.
6. Lint, the three checks, the derivation script and the Lean build give
   what they gave before.

A job that fails a check goes back to its worker with the failing lines.
